reading: the corner inequality primesum <= P0+A0 holds (margin>=0) for TRUE primes;
slack quantifies tightness. pow2 dominating primesum explains §372b (5% Lambda(2) bend flips
the margin negative). The RH content at the corner = why the TRUE Lambda keeps primesum just
under P0+A0 while a small bend exceeds it — an explicit inequality on q_n-weighted prime sums.
